From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Taron <philip.taron@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/intel: add MSI MPG X670E Carbon to the codec
 denylist

The AMD Ryzen HD-audio controller (1022:15e3) on the MSI MPG X670E Carbon
WIFI (MS-7D70) is exposed with no codec attached: STATESTS reads back 0 on
every boot, so azx registers an empty card and logs "no codecs found!".
The board's actual audio is provided by a separate MSI USB audio device.

This is the same situation already handled for the MSI X870E Tomahawk, which
shares the 1022:15e3 controller. Gate it behind a DMI board-name match for
the same reason: the PCI subsystem ID alone could collide with other boards.

Signed-off-by: Philip Taron <philip.taron@gmail.com>
---
 sound/hda/controllers/intel.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/hda/controllers/intel.c b/sound/hda/controllers/intel.c
index a4104376523a..02e09d8f282f 100644
--- a/sound/hda/controllers/intel.c
+++ b/sound/hda/controllers/intel.c
@@ -2093,6 +2093,11 @@ static struct pci_device_id driver_denylist_msi_x870e[] = {
 	{}
 };

+static struct pci_device_id driver_denylist_msi_x670e_carbon[] = {
+	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(0x1022, 0x15e3, 0x1462, 0xed70) }, /* MSI MPG X670E Carbon WiFi */
+	{}
+};
+
 /* DMI-based denylist, to be used when:
  *  - PCI subsystem IDs are zero, impossible to distinguish from valid sound cards.
  *  - Different modifications of the same laptop use different GPU models.
@@ -2114,6 +2119,14 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id driver_denylist_dmi[] = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = &driver_denylist_msi_x870e,
 	},
+	{
+		/* PCI device matching alone incorrectly matches some laptops */
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "Micro-Star International Co., Ltd."),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "MPG X670E CARBON WIFI (MS-7D70)"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &driver_denylist_msi_x670e_carbon,
+	},
 	{}
 };

